#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(export)s was exported to the grid but your solar (and battery) data "
"does not account for it, so the household consumption and self-"
"sufficiency could not be reconstructed reliably and are hidden. This "
"usually means a solar sensor is not reporting all of your production, or "
"a battery is not mapped. Check your data sources."
msgstr ""
"%(export)s was exported to the grid but your solar (and battery) data "
"does not account for it, so the household consumption and self-"
"sufficiency could not be reconstructed reliably and are hidden. This "
"usually means a solar sensor is not reporting all of your production, or "
"a battery is not mapped. Check your data sources."

#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(export)s was exported to the grid, but you have not supplied any solar "
"data — so the household consumption and self-sufficiency could not be "
"reconstructed reliably and are hidden. A meter does not export energy the"
" house did not generate, so either you do have solar panels (answer "
"\"yes\" above and map the sensor), or an existing battery is feeding the "
"grid and is not mapped."
msgstr ""
"%(export)s was exported to the grid, but you have not supplied any solar "
"data — so the household consumption and self-sufficiency could not be "
"reconstructed reliably and are hidden. A meter does not export energy the"
" house did not generate, so either you do have solar panels (answer "
"\"yes\" above and map the sensor), or an existing battery is feeding the "
"grid and is not mapped."

